      "writtenOn": "2025-02-21T20:10:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like a very specialized function which can\u0027t be used for anything else. Can we instead make get_track() an exported function and change this function to `for_each_kmem_cache_object()` which loops over all slab objects calling the `fn` callback? Something like:\n```\nfor_each_kmem_cache_object()\n{\n    for_each_kmem_cache_node() {\n        list_for_each_entry(slab, \u0026n-\u003epartial, slab_list) {\n            for_each_object(p, s, slab_address(slab), slab-\u003eobjects) {\n                fn(s, p, t-\u003eaddr, handle, private);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
      "range": {
